# Input
```
-- A temporal primary key (Postgres 18) needs a GiST index, so USING INDEX is no alternative
-- expect_lint/addingPrimaryKeyConstraint
ALTER TABLE bookings ADD CONSTRAINT bookings_pkey PRIMARY KEY (room_id, during WITHOUT OVERLAPS);

```

# Diagnostics
lint/addingPrimaryKeyConstraint ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × Adding a PRIMARY KEY constraint results in locks and table rewrites.
  
  i Adding a PRIMARY KEY constraint requires an ACCESS EXCLUSIVE lock which blocks reads.
  
  i There is no concurrent alternative for a temporal key (WITHOUT OVERLAPS). Use SET lock_timeout to limit the impact on concurrent operations.
